// aug03 reactive divergence_000000 (2026-08-04): INTERP-side missed
// becoming-selected fire — the JIT was right. On a guard-flip
// re-selection the scrutinee produces nothing, and the wake bound the
// pattern var with Tag::STALE (the 2026-07-18 bind-tag ruling read
// too broadly): the interpolation "[v0]" produced a STALE "2", the
// str::len CallSite's any-arg-fired dispatch gate refused, the woken
// arm's cache stayed empty, and the select emitted NOTHING while the
// kernel's selection-memory fire produced len("2")=1 (interp 1;2 vs
// jit 1;1 for v6-v0). Every simpler body shape masked it: bare v0 /
// bare "[v0]" have no dispatch gate; str::len("hello") has an
